</patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>None</text><sources><source name="APP" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1177954A1</text><sources><source name="APP" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOKAI RIKA CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KABUSHIKI KAISHA TOKAI-RIKA-DENKI-SEISAKUSHO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ASAGIRI KATSUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUMIYASHIKI AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ASAGIRI, KATSUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUMIYASHIKI, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A webbing winder intended to attain lightweight while ensuring lock strength. Held in a storing portion (40) formed in the holder (24C) of a base lock (24) is a single lock plate (42) that meshes with an internal ratchet (38) during the quick vehicle deceleration.  During the quick vehicle deceleration, a lock plate (42) is moved as guided by a guide hole (50) formed in a V gear (46) and meshes with the internal ratchet (38). Further, with the then-produced reaction utilized, the holder (24c) of the base lock (24) is pressed against the internal ratchet (38), and plastically deformed for engagement. Thus, a state of locking with the internal ratchet (38) is established at two radially opposite locations.  Moreover, since only a single lock plate (42) is used, it is possible to attain lightweight while ensuring lock strength.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Enrouleur à sangle conçu pour être léger tout en assurant un blocage fiable. Un mécanisme de verrouillage de base (24) renferme, dans une partie de stockage (40) formée dans le support (24C), une seule plaque de verrouillage (42) qui s'engrène avec un rochet interne (38) lors d'une décélération brutale du véhicule. La plaque de verrouillage (42) se déplace, guidée par un trou de guidage (50) formé dans une roue pour courroie trapézoïdale (46), et s'engrène avec le rochet interne (38). La réaction produite provoque la poussée du support (24C) du mécanisme de verrouillage (24) contre le rochet interne (38) et une déformation plastique qui permet le contact. Il s'établit ainsi un état de verrouillage avec le rochet interne (38) à deux emplacements opposés. L'utilisation d'une seule plaque de verrouillage permet de produire un enrouleur léger assurant un blocage fiable.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>